# Multi-100MB YCSB-style bench traces and procedural workload dumps that blow
# past GitHub's 100 MB single-file ceiling. Generator scripts + spec are what
# should be tracked; the traces are reproducible from them.
setup/iter17A_single_key_flood/
setup/*_single_key_flood/
**/*.spec_load
**/*.spec_trans
**/bench_single_key_flood_*

# Run-time noise: program stdout/stderr captures, run logs, and zero-replacement
# backup files. Iter summaries (*.md) carry the analysis; the raw streams stay
# local for reproducibility. Note: pre-existing tracked .log/.out/.err files in
# HEAD are unaffected — gitignore only blocks new additions.
*.log
*.out
*.err
*.bak
